1
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Warriors. Conquerors. Heroes.

2
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:46,000
The Barbarians is a adventure, fantasy, action film directed by Ruggero Deodato.

3
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Orphaned brothers Kutchek and Gore are adopted by a tribe
led by Canary the owner of a powerful jewel.

4
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:26,000
The evil Kadar wants both Canary and the jewel.

5
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:16,000
Attacking the tribe he kidnaps Canary but the stone eludes him.

6
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
The brothers are taken to be trained as gladiators and
years later have grown to be VERY big.

7
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:56,000
They escape and set off on a quest to find the jewel and rescue Canary.

8
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Kutchek, played by Peter Paul.

9
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:36,000
Gore, played by David Paul.

10
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:26,000
Kadar, played by Richard Lynch.

11
00:53:10,000 --> 00:53:16,000
Kara/Ismene, played by Eva LaRue.

12
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Canary, played by Virginia Bryant.

13
01:02:50,000 --> 01:02:56,000
China, played by Sheeba Alahani.

14
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:46,000
The Barbarians is a 1987 sword and sorcery film directed by Ruggero Deodato and starring
the Barbarian Brothers (Peter and David Paul), Richard Lynch and Eva La Rue.

15
01:12:30,000 --> 01:12:36,000
The film is an Italian and American co-production
shot in Rome and the Abruzzo Mountains.

16
01:17:20,000 --> 01:17:26,000
Peter and David Paul were nominated for a Golden Raspberry Award for Worst
New Star for this film at the 8th Golden Raspberry Awards.

17
01:22:10,000 --> 01:22:16,000
The film explores themes of dragon, barbarian, twins, jewel, sword and sorcery.
